---
layout: layout.njk
permalink: /interviews/
title: Interviews
description: Jamie in his own words. Thingy asks, Jamie answers out loud, one session at a time, and the transcript is edited from speech for reading.
---
{%- from "macros.njk" import thingyHead %}
{#- The interview sessions (content/interviews/session-N.md), newest first: a session's number, its point in Thingy's
    voice, and one line of Jamie's from it (`pull` in the front matter, held to the transcript by tests/quotes.test.ts).
    Then the index by thing, and what no question has reached yet. A transcript is a source, the way a post is: the
    pages quote it and link the question. #}
<section class="intro has-character">
  <a class="thingy-companion" href="/things/thingy-model/" aria-label="Meet Thingy’s character"><img src="https://thingy.thingelstad.xyz/character/latest/poses/workshop-thinking-curious.webp" width="170" height="170" alt="Thingy, the Workshop Builder, turning a question over" /></a>
  <h1>Interviews</h1>
  <p class="lede">From time to time Thingy sits down with Jamie and asks about what he has built. Each session has one point Thingy wanted to get to. The question numbers keep running from one session to the next. The answers are Jamie’s words, edited from speech for reading.</p>
</section>
<div class="session-list">
  {% for interview in site.interviews %}
  <article class="session-card{% if loop.first %} is-latest{% endif %}">
    <a class="session-number" href="{{ interview.page }}" aria-label="Session {{ interview.session }}">{{ interview.session }}</a>
    <div class="session-what">
      <p class="meta">Session {{ interview.session }} · {{ interview.started | date }} · {{ interview.questions | length }} questions</p>
      <h2><a href="{{ interview.page }}">{{ interview.title }}</a></h2>
      <div class="thingy-line">{{ thingyHead() }}<p class="thingy-says">{{ interview.point }}</p></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="session-pull" aria-label="From session {{ interview.session }}">
      <blockquote class="pull">“<a href="{{ interview.page }}#q{{ interview.pull.n }}">{{ interview.pull.words }}</a>”</blockquote>
      <p class="who"><img src="{{ owner.avatar }}" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" /><span>Jamie, question {{ interview.pull.n }}</span></p>
    </aside>
  </article>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
<section class="interview-find" id="find-a-thing" aria-labelledby="find-a-thing-title">
  <h2 id="find-a-thing-title">Find a thing</h2>
  <p class="meta">The {{ site.interviewIndex | length }} things he has been asked about. Each number is a session, and it leads to the first question there about that thing.</p>
  <ul class="interview-index">
    {% for row in site.interviewIndex %}<li><a href="{{ row.thing.page }}">{{ row.thing.title }}</a><span class="interview-index-sessions">{% for s in row.sessions %}<a href="{{ s.page }}" aria-label="{{ row.thing.title }} in session {{ s.session }}, question {{ s.n }}">{{ s.session }}</a>{% endfor %}</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
{% if site.stillToAsk | length %}
<section class="still-to-ask" id="still-to-ask" aria-labelledby="still-to-ask-title">
  <h2 id="still-to-ask-title">Still to ask</h2>
  <div>
    <p class="muted">The things no session has reached yet, worked out from the registry when the site builds.</p>
    <p>{% for thing in site.stillToAsk %}<a class="tag" href="{{ thing.page }}">{{ thing.title }}</a> {% endfor %}</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
